From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StellarSeal <emnoigi1452@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:18:54 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 089/143] Index scheduled block ticks by chunk and current-tick
 membership

WorldServer.a(Chunk, boolean) walked every pending scheduled tick (and the current batch) for each chunk save, and a(BlockPosition, Block) did a linear List.contains over the current tick batch (up to 65,536 entries) on every repeater/comparator neighbor update.

- ChunkIndexedTreeSet replaces HashTreeSet for nextTickList: same equals-based contains, same compareTo order, plus a per-chunk-column index so the save query touches only the 4 columns its [x0-2, x0+16) x [z0-2, z0+16) box can reach. Results, order and half-open bounds are unchanged. add() refuses an equal entry, replacing the contains()+add() pair.
- MultiplicitySet mirrors the current batch W for O(1) isBlockTickPending checks.
- No config toggle: behavior is identical (verified against a verbatim copy of the old logic over randomized operations).

Measured (best of 4, JDK 21, ScheduledTickIndexPerfTest):
- chunk-save query, 100k ticks / 2025 chunks, 64 saves: 466 ms -> 2.8 ms (~170x; 755-917x on quieter runs)
- isBlockTickPending, 20k batch / 2000 probes: 172 ms -> 0.25 ms (~700x)
- schedule+drain of 200k ticks: 365 ms -> 496 ms (0.74x). The index costs ~0.6 us per scheduled tick; accepted in exchange for the above.

Credit: per-chunk scheduled tick indexing follows the approach of modern Paper (Spottedleaf / PaperMC); implementation is original for 1.12.2.

